{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaOddParityAvatarReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaOddParityAvatarReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_avatar_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_avatar_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaOddParityAvatarReduction.lean#L81-L94","doc":"**Reduction at the c_2 = −1 baseline.** With `a₂ = −1` (the\n`cos(√2·u)` baseline truncated through u³), the avatar product is\n\n  `(1 − u²)(1 + g u³) = 1 − u² + g u³ − g u⁵`,\n\nso the u² coefficient is `−1` (independent of `g`, matching the proved\nN=2 rung) and the u³ coefficient is exactly `g`. A non-fitted closure of\nc_3 therefore demands a closed-form `g(q)` reproducing the cal-anchored\nc_3 target — the saturated single-formula search. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_c3_content_eq_g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_c3_content_eq_g","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaOddParityAvatarReduction.lean#L71-L79","doc":"**The odd-parity content collapses to g·u³.** Subtracting the even\nbaseline `1 + a₂u²` and the residual `a₂ g u⁵` from the product leaves\nexactly `g·u³`: the entire order-u³ (c_3) content is the single scalar\n`g`, independent of the baseline coefficient `a₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_avatar_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_odd_parity_avatar_product","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaOddParityAvatarReduction.lean#L55-L69","doc":"**Odd-parity avatar product (general even baseline).** The product\nof an even baseline `1 + a₂·u²` (carrying the u² coefficient `a₂`, and\nno u¹/u³ term — the through-u³ truncation of an even function) with the\nminimal odd extension `1 + g·u³` expands exactly as\n\n  `(1 + a₂u²)(1 + g u³) = 1 + a₂u² + g u³ + a₂ g u⁵`.\n\nReading coefficients: the u² coefficient is `a₂` (contains no `g`), and\nthe u³ coefficient is `g`. There is no u⁴ term; the only higher term is\n`a₂ g u⁵`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}